2. BANKED c2=c4=0 ANCHOR (base AeST, scalar live) -- wf3_eta_K_final.out
==========================================================================
  eta_K = (K_B J_Y + 2)/(J_Y + 1),  alpha_1 = -4 eta_K,  alpha_3 = 0
  [PASS] J_Y -> oo recovers pure-EA -4K_B
  [PASS] J_Y = 1 gives -2(K_B+2)
  [PASS] all 10 banked wf3 grid values alpha_1(0) reproduced by -4 eta_K
  => generalized solve at c2=c4=0 MUST return alpha_1 = -4(K_B J_Y+2)/(J_Y+1); e.g. (K_B,J_Y)=(1/5,1): -22/5
  The decisive unknown: d eta_K / d c4 at fixed K_B, J_Y=1 -- does the '+2' (scalar drag) scale with c14?
  If eta_K(c4) = (c14 J_Y + 2)/(J_Y+1) [drag c4-blind]  -> alpha_1 -> -4 at c14->0: DEAD for all c2,c4.
  If eta_K(c4) = c14 (J_Y + 2/K_B)/(J_Y+1) [drag ~ c14] -> zero only at c14=0: instantaneous, DEAD.
  Only a c4-dependence that is NOT proportional to c14 and crosses zero at 0<c14<2 can pass. NOT-COMPUTED.

